; The network's interrupt, word 100 <6>, the Chaosnet interface's request: the
; microcode writes the CSR, word 140, 0 as a stray, which turns both interrupt
; enables off and drops the level (sys/ucadr/uc-interrupt.lisp,
; INTR-NETWORK-STRAY; QUUX's Ethernet contract, section 8, step R3).  Load
; lisp/network-stray.lisp first; it wants a band without the NCP, on revision
; 15 or 16, which have the interface.  Microcode without the stray dismisses
; the interrupt untouched, and the level, never cleared, interrupts again at
; once for ever: the case that enables the transmit interrupt never answers.
; NTS-STATE is (the CSR's enables <5:4>, its Transmit Done <7>, word 100 <6>).
;
; Precondition: the enables off, the transmitter idle (Transmit Done up), no
; request.
(nts-state) => (0 1 0)
; The control: the receive interrupt enable alone, no packet received, raises
; no request, and the CSR keeps it; then off again.
(nts-enable #o20) => (1 1 0)
(nts-enable 0) => (0 1 0)
; The stray: the transmit interrupt enable with Transmit Done up requests at
; once, and the stray writes the CSR 0.  Twice, then both enables.
(nts-enable #o40) => (0 1 0)
(nts-enable #o40) => (0 1 0)
(nts-enable #o60) => (0 1 0)
